  "articleBody": "Dealing with interior storm damage is stressful, and it's easy to make a few common mistakes that can complicate recovery. First off, never enter an unsafe area. If you suspect structural damage, gas leaks, or electrical hazards, stay out and call for help. Your safety is paramount! Another frequent misstep is starting permanent repairs before the damage is fully documented and assessed by your insurance company. Always take thorough photos and videos and get your insurer's approval before major work begins. Don't throw away damaged items or receipts for temporary repairs; you'll need these for your claim. It's also a mistake to just hire the first contractor who shows up. Always check their licensing, insurance, and make sure they have experience with storm damage. Ask for a detailed, written estimate that clearly separates temporary mitigation from full restoration. Rushing into decisions or not asking enough questions can lead to more headaches down the line. Take a breath, secure your property safely, document everything, and then carefully choose your path forward. HH Remodeling LLC is here to help guide you through these crucial steps.",
